From 15d90f0335141c5856140f16c5e312b2ae9f10cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 02:52:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: max17042_battery: report the battery's design
 capacity

charge_full_design reads the DesignCap register. The driver programs
that register from the battery info only on the MAX17055 (and on the
others only with platform config data at a power-on reset), so on a
MAX17042 described in DT it shows whatever the bootloader or the chip
left. On a Samsung Galaxy Tab 2 10.1, whose 7000 mAh battery is
described in DT, it reads 9419 mAh, while FullCAP (charge_full) has
learned about 3.9 Ah on the aged pack: userspace can't compute the
battery's health from that.

Report the design capacity of the monitored battery when there is one,
and the register otherwise.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c b/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
index 505a68c26463..d9c7a418e6f2 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
@@ -357,6 +357,17 @@ static int max17042_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 		val->intval = data >> 8;
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL_DESIGN:
+		/*
+		 * DesignCap is programmed from the battery info on the MAX17055
+		 * only; on the others it holds whatever the bootloader or a
+		 * platform config left there, so prefer the described battery.
+		 */
+		if (psy->battery_info &&
+		    psy->battery_info->charge_full_design_uah > 0) {
+			val->intval = psy->battery_info->charge_full_design_uah;
+			break;
+		}
+
 		ret = regmap_read(map, MAX17042_DesignCap, &data);
 		if (ret < 0)
 			return ret;
